<Project>

  <!--
    CVE-2025-6965 (GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q) flags SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3 (the native SQLite bundle,
    SQLite < 3.50.2), a transitive dependency of Microsoft.Data.Sqlite used by the SQLite database
    driver. Every released SQLitePCLRaw version (through 2.1.11, the newest) is flagged and no patched
    bundle has shipped yet. The flaw requires attacker-controlled aggregate SQL (more aggregate terms
    than columns); Switchboard only ever issues the parameterized CRUD statements it constructs
    itself, so it is not reachable. Suppress the NuGet audit warning solution-wide (it otherwise
    surfaces on every project that transitively references the driver) until an upstream bundle ships
    SQLite >= 3.50.2, then remove this suppression and update the package.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
